_model: proposition
---
title: Proposition 6
---
order: 6
---
short_label: IV.6
---
statement: To inscribe a square in a given circle.
---
red_highlight: yes
---
proof:

Let *ABCD* be the given circle.

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="canvas_0" width="290" height="290" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<noscript><img alt="IV.6 diagram" src="propIV6.gif"/></noscript>
<script type="text/javascript">
    geomlib.init({
        canvasid: "canvas_0",
        background: "35,19,100",
        title: "IV.6",
        pivot: "E",
        elements: [
            "A;point;free;145,30",
            "C;point;free;145,260",
            "E;point;midpoint;A,C;black;green",
            "ABCD;circle;radius;E,A;0;0;black;random",
            "B;point;perpendicular;E,A",
            "D;point;perpendicular;E,C",
            "square;polygon;quadrilateral;A,B,C,D;0;0;black;random",
            "AC;line;connect;A,C",
            "BD;line;connect;B,D"
        ],
    });
</script>
</figure>

It is required to inscribe a square in the circle *ABCD.*

Draw two diameters *AC* and *BD* of the circle *ABCD* at right angles to one another, and join *AB, BC, CD,* and *DA.* [!just III.1, I.11]

Then, since *BE* equals *ED,* for *E* is the center, and *EA* is common and at right angles, therefore the base *AB* equals the base *AD.* [!just I.4]

For the same reason each of the straight lines *BC* and *CD* also equals each of the straight lines *AB* and *AD.* Therefore the quadrilateral *ABCD* is equilateral.

I say next that it is also right-angled.

For, since the straight line *BD* is a diameter of the circle *ABCD,* therefore *BAD* is a semicircle, therefore the angle *BAD* is right. [!just III.31]

For the same reason each of the angles *ABC, BCD,* and *CDA* is also right. Therefore the quadrilateral *ABCD* is right-angled.

But it was also proved equilateral, therefore it is a square, and it has been inscribed in the circle *ABCD.*

Therefore the square *ABCD* has been inscribed in the given circle.

<div class="qed">Q.E.F.</div>
<br clear="all">
---
body:

This construction is used in a few propositions of Book XII, the first being @XII.2.
